# Fixed-shape content-invalid controllers

These new pieces consume the already computed canonical P0 output and generated
transcript. They do not create P0 or establish the enclosing request protocol.
The intended invalid-content family is VOTE with fixed list count3..1000 and
valid bounded field lengths. Arbitrary role/row/length dispatch remains open.
REG can keep the ordinary always-valid route; this introduces no new REG error.

P0 output is exactly60bits: valid1, error_code3, order_index16, actual_count16,
declared_count16 and vote_value8. Its source first-error order is retained by
copying the existing error payload, not recomputing validation in the wrapper.
The field-copy tests include every code payload. The size-error variant is not
reachable for the intended count3..1000 family; testing its copy is not evidence
that out-of-range shape dispatch has been implemented.

`ValidatedWrites` takes the ordinary ProgrammedWrites inputs plus one borrowed
valid bit. It keeps the original source field offsets; log and workspace shift
by one. The first two enable computations are valid; the primary ones are valid
AND source S0flag. All M+2 framed record scans, including inactive primary slots,
still run. Domain bytes, actual trial counter, padded staging, chronological
slot order and append inverse are unchanged. Scatter is undone around each
append. There are no added oracle calls or work bits: the valid bit is an input.

Relative to the ordinary W cost its exact change is

```
X: -4
CNOT: +4-2M
Toffoli: +2M.
```

When valid is zero, every append enable is zero and the entire log and counter
are identity, even for a full canonical log and arbitrary supplied primary
flags. When valid is one, the original S0/capacity premises apply. Inverse
traversal reverses primary entries and then challenge2/challenge1, using the
append's actual decrement-before-reversal circuit.

`ValidatedReturn` receives P0[60] followed by ReturnProjection's exhaustion bit
and field inputs. It computes the clean E map into a fresh temporary output,
forms !valid in one clean bit, and copies E's complete output conditioned on
valid. E's exhaustion bit is the low result-tag bit; !valid is the high bit.
The tag is0 for proof,1 for exhaustion and2 for a P0 error. A separate59-bit
payload copies P0's error fields conditioned on !valid. Last32, length64 and
proof remain in E's source order. The result is a mathematical sum-type
register, not Rust enum memory or a new serialized wire protocol.

The same E map then clears its temporary output; the invalid flag is cleared.
For arbitrary caller targets this is an XOR map. Therefore a zero contribution
on rejection preserves a nonzero caller target; on zero initialized result
registers it produces canonical zero proof, length and exhaustion-last fields.
All source basis labels are unchanged, while their reduced state may be
entangled with outputs as for other clean maps.

If E has cost C, output width o and one clean work bit, the wrapper has

```
cost = 2C + (o+59) Toffoli + 2 X + 3 CNOT
clean work = o+2
input bits = E.inputs+60
output bits = E.outputs+60.
```

This includes all temp preparation and cleanup; it makes no F call. The
arbitrary intermediate generator work on rejection may be discarded only by
actually running the matching inverse with unchanged input registers and the
same immutable F. No adversary may interleave inside the atomic request.
Programmed writes are disabled on rejection, so after copying only the P0
error the generator's net action cancels jointly with the oracle and reference
registers. This argument needs the actual totalized generator/controller join;
these helpers alone do not establish it or claim complete resources.

The39 focused controls cover valid chronology/inverse, invalid full-log identity,
exact census in both directions, each P0 payload and both exhaustion values,
arbitrary caller targets, clean temporary state, missing-uncompute/wrong-enable
negative controls, strict API refusals, and static actual-row/role accounting.
No production elementary circuit, Rust build, physical workspace or hardware
qualification was executed. All complete and qualification flags remain false.
